# Build context exclusions.
#
# The Docker build context is the repository root. Without this file Docker
# transfers the entire tree (including node_modules, which is hundreds of MB of
# symlinks that are useless in the image and can break inside the build).
#
# Every COPY in docker/Dockerfile names an exact path, so nothing here is needed
# by the build. These patterns are defence in depth plus a large speed-up.

# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local state and caches
data
.pnpm-store
.wrangler
**/.wrangler

# Secrets — must never enter a build context
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*

# Databases
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# VCS, docs and test artefacts that the image does not need
.git
.gitignore
docs
tests
*.log
.DS_Store
